+++ b/docs/evidence/renderer/pbr-fog-ab-20261020/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+# Hi02 nebula render smoke: PBR and legacy (2026-10-20)
+
+Two NAP-only Release-client runs loaded the same Hi02 test save and captured
+the first non-cutscene space frame after 120 loaded space frames. Both reached
+`UI: Interface loaded`, entered `Hi02`, and wrote a 640x480 readback without a
+renderer exception. The client resolution was 640x360. The active snapshot
+contains 14 NAP packages; the archive sizes and SHA-256 values were checked
+against `active.json`. The archived NAP inputs are staged under
+`Data/NAP/.runtime-test-stage/illum-detail-hdr-20261019/` and the application
+tree has no loose Freelancer `DATA` directory.
+
+The render target used SDL3's `offscreen` video driver and Mesa OpenGL 4.3. The
+reported renderer string is `NVE7`. `LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=1` did not override
+the selected graphics device, so this is not identified as llvmpipe. It is
+also not a validation on the Intel HD 4600 or RTX 5060.
+
+## Captures
+
+![PBR and legacy material nebula captures](hi02-fog-comparison.png)
+
+| Capture | Render settings |
+|---|---|
+| [PBR/HDR](fog-pbr-on.png) | Normal maps, Surface PBR maps, generated tangents, environment maps, diffuse IBL and HDR on |
+| [Legacy/HDR](fog-legacy.png) | Those PBR and environment-map options off; HDR on |
+
+Bloom, SSAO, shadows, soft particles, particle effects and dynamic lighting
+were off in both runs. Both frames show the Hi02 nebula backdrop and the planet
+scene; neither run crashed while drawing the scene. The active manifest is
+[`active.json`](active.json), and the full runtime logs are
+[PBR](run-pbr.log.txt) and [legacy](run-legacy.log.txt). Start options are
+recorded in [`launch-options.txt`](launch-options.txt). The capture hashes are:
+
+| File | SHA-256 |
+|---|---|
+| `fog-pbr-on.png` | `5b372cdb74862c6bfa7501d9f1e4f418c2b1babdf98f137555febc2f7859b16d` |
+| `fog-legacy.png` | `4fb659d78b012fe10c7378ad7ad6089bedc8f853faf60804a46684e13cd64c79` |
+
+## Limits
+
+These are separate live simulation frames, not a synchronized pixel A/B.
+Camera orientation, weapon fire and other moving effects differ between them.
+The images confirm that the PBR shader path renders the nebula scene after the
+fog change and that the legacy path still renders it; they do not isolate the
+fog equation or calibrate fog color and distance. A paused, fixed-camera
+material A/B and retail comparison remain open.
